    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence presents a genuinely balanced situation for AAPL. The bull case is supported by verifiable facts: a confirmed uptrend with a fresh golden cross (50 SMA crossing above 200 SMA on June 14), strong momentum (MACD positive at 1.72), exceptional cash generation ($62.6B operating cash flow in six months), and a 19% sixty-day gain on expanding volume. However, the bear case is equally grounded in the same data: RSI at 75.88 is deeply overbought, price is pinned to the upper Bollinger Band ($210.48 vs. $210.96), and valuation at ~25.6x operating cash flow is rich. With no sentiment/news data available to break the tie and no fundamental catalyst justifying aggressive accumulation at this statistical extreme of a parabolic move, maintaining the position at current levels is the appropriate action. The plan calls for holding at ~$210.48, watching for a pullback toward the 10 EMA ($201.77) for a better entry, or a decisive close above $218.12 to confirm continuation.\n\n**Entry Price**: 210.48\n\n**Stop Loss**: 194.18\n\n**Position Sizing**: Neutral/benchmark weight; do not concentrate beyond normal portfolio weight. Reserve dry powder for a pullback entry near the 10 EMA ($201.77) or VWMA ($199.52).\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
